  "explains": "invoice_total in app/services/ledger.py changes. ledger.py is imported by name (from app.services.ledger import all_totals, invoice_total, mark_void, new_invoice) by the handler module app/handlers/invoices.py, and by the unit test tests/test_ledger.py, which is a test and never a caller. In the handler module only get_invoice uses invoice_total (list_invoices uses all_totals, create_invoice new_invoice, void_invoice mark_void), so the walk reaches get_invoice and with it the route of operationId getInvoice, GET /v1/invoices/{invoiceId}. The chain of the screen shows the way: the import of ledger in the handler module and the line where get_invoice uses invoice_total, then the client line in the web app (fetchInvoice calls getInvoice), the import of fetchInvoice in the page, the import of the page in the routes file and its Route.",
  "complete_for": [
    "changed_symbol",
    "caller",
    "unit_test",
    "route",
    "http_edge",
    "screen"
  ],
